#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# indexed

#% text
# `indexed(x, i)` is the part of the list `x` at the index `i`; `indexed(x, [i, j, ...])` is the part along the path of indices.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `indexed(x, i)` equals `x[i]` for a list `x` and an integer `i` in range.

#% item
# For a symbol `x` it stays `indexed(x, i)`: a symbolic vector `x` can have components `indexed(x, 1)`, `indexed(x, 2)`, ...

#% item
# `indexed(x, [i, j])` is the same as `extract(x, [i, j])`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
indexed([a, b], 1)
#% output
#= a

#% cell
indexed(x, 1)
#% output
#= indexed(x, 1)

#% cell
indexed([[a, b, c], [d, e, f]], [1, 2])
#% output
#= b

#% cell
indexed([a, b, c], -1)
#% output
#= c

#% cell
indexed(x, [1, 2])
#% output
#= indexed(x, [1, 2])

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `extract`, `part`
